From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-rg <linux-rg@local>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sched/bore: finish the 7.2 placement hunks

On 7.2.7 the 0001 fair.c hunks for place_entity and
requeue_delayed_entity reject, and 0002 leaves two pieces of the BORE
6.8 behaviour that CachyOS carries for 7.2 unapplied:

- place_entity keeps upstream's early vslice computation, so a task
  that BORE sends straight to vslice_found (futex waiter) still gets a
  full slice. Start vslice at 0 and compute it only on the normal path.
- requeue_delayed_entity does not mark the placement as a wakeup, so
  BORE's halved wakeup slice never applies to a requeued delayed task.
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -6017,13 +6017,12 @@
 static void
 place_entity(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq, struct sched_entity *se, int flags)
 {
-	u64 vslice, vruntime = avg_vruntime(cfs_rq);
+	u64 vslice = 0, vruntime = avg_vruntime(cfs_rq);
 	bool update_zero = false;
 	s64 lag = 0;
 
 	if (!se->custom_slice)
 		se->slice = sysctl_sched_base_slice;
-	vslice = calc_delta_fair(se->slice, se);
 
 	/*
 	 * Due to how V is constructed as the weighted average of entities,
@@ -7849,6 +7848,10 @@
 		cfs_rq->nr_queued--;
 		if (se != cfs_rq->curr)
 			__dequeue_entity(cfs_rq, se);
+#ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
+		if (static_branch_likely(&sched_bore_key))
+			flags |= ENQUEUE_WAKEUP;
+#endif /* CONFIG_SCHED_BORE */
 		place_entity(cfs_rq, se, flags);
 		if (se != cfs_rq->curr)
 			__enqueue_entity(cfs_rq, se);
-- 
